    "name" : "LICENSED_CAPACITY",
    "dataTypeName" : "number",
    "description" : "The total number of children that a program can serve at a given time. Note: 1) Licensed capacity by age is not available for Family Child Care programs or Group and School Age programs with a capacity of 10 or fewer children. 2) Family Child Care programs' license capacity usually start at 6 and vary between 6-10. In some cases, a program cannot be approved to care for 6 children due to factors such as lack of sufficient space. 3) Classrooms in Group and School Age programs often overlap age groups, so capacity by age will not equal licensed capacity. For instance, if a preschool program uses the same space as the after-school school-age program, both preschool and after school capacities would be listed, but both groups cannot be in attendance at the same time because they occupy the same space, so licensed capacity would be lower than the sum of capacity by age.",
